voting turnout by county, as reported by the counties)"},"notes":["Diagnostic only: nothing here feeds the forecast.","Texas has no party registration and the SOS publishes no party data: these are turnout counts, not vote choice. No party split is estimated (modelled party scores are proprietary and not used).","Early votes = cumulative in-person early votes + cumulative mail ballots received, as reported by each county to the SOS; shares are of the registered voters in the same file. Mail ballots received are not mail ballots accepted.","Mail voting in Texas is limited to voters 65 or older, voters with a disability, voters out of the county during the election, voters confined for childbirth and eligible jailed voters (Election Code ch. 82), so mail is a small and old-skewed slice of the early vote; mail ballots keep arriving after early voting ends and are not followed here.","Same-day comparison: day k of early voting in 2026 (Oct 19-30) against day k in 2022 (Oct 24 - Nov 4). Both periods start on the 17th day before Election Day moved to the following Monday, run 12 days and end on the 4th day before Election Day, so day k is the same weekday and the same number of days out in both years.","Rules since 2022: SB 1 (2021: 6 a.m.-10 p.m. window, no 24-hour or drive-through voting, ID numbers on mail ballots) already applied in 2022. HB 1217 (2023) extends the 12-hour last-week weekdays and the last-weekend hours to every county regardless of population (in 2022 only larger counties had to offer them), which adds hours mostly in small rural counties. SB 2753 (2025) is not in effect for November 2026 (SOS calendar: Oct 19-30).","County roster updates lag: a county that has not sent the day's file shows the previous total. Each day lists how many counties did not move from the day before; the SOS revises past days as counties catch up, and the latest version of every day is used.","Registered voters grew between 2022 and 2026, so turnout is compared as a share of registered voters, and the group composition (its share of the statewide early vote) is shown against its 2022 share."]},"turnout":{"generated":"2026-10-30T07:45Z","election_day":"2026-11-03","reference":{"chosen":"A","rms_log":{"A":0.186,"B":0.6307,"C":0.5676},"n":4,"leads":[15,7]},"level":0.8,"min_midterms":3,"states":[{"state":"NC","label":"North Carolina","through":"2026-10-28","days_out":6,"banked":2150016,"same_point_2022":1585987,"vs_2022_same_point_pct":35.6,"total_2022":3773924,"share_of_2022_total_pct":57.0,"projection":{"n_midterm":1,"midterm_errors_pct":{"2022":-0.7},"presidential_errors_pct":{"2012":5.0,"2016":7.6,"2020":42.4,"2024":-9.2},"reason":"1 comparable past midterm at this point: too few to test a projection"},"onestop_opened_days_out":{"2008":19,"2010":19,"2012":19,"2014":12,"2016":19,"2018":20,"2020":19,"2022":19,"2024":19,"2026":19}},{"state":"PA","label":"Pennsylvania","through":"2026-10-28","days_out":6,"banked":968855,"same_point_2022":1003823,"vs_2022_same_point_pct":-3.5,"total_2022":5368021,"share_of_2022_total_pct":18.0,"projection":{"n_midterm":0,"midterm_errors_pct":{},"presidential_errors_pct":{"2024":-24.4},"reason":"0 comparable past midterms at this point: too few to test a projection"}},{"state":"GA","through":"2026-10-28","days_out":6,"banked":2308779,"same_point_2022":2097540,"vs_2022_same_point_pct":10.1,"total_2022":3935924,"share_of_2022_total_pct":58.7,"label":"Georgia"},{"state":"FL","through":"2026-10-29","days_out":5,"banked":3896794,"same_point_2022":null,"vs_2022_same_point_pct":null,"total_2022":7758014,"note":"mail and in-person early ballots on their latest compiles; no 2022 file at this point","share_of_2022_total_pct":50.2,"label":"Florida"},{"state":"NV","through":"2026-10-29","days_out":5,"banked":466081,"mail":279427,"in_person":186654,"mail_2022_same_point":202271,"mail_vs_2022_same_point_pct":38.1,"total_2022":null,"note":"Clark County only; mail is the only part with a 2022 file at the same point","label":"